Description: musl support for the V8 base platform layer
 The default thread stack size is only raised above the musl default (128kB)
 on AIX and Darwin, so V8 threads overflow the stack early on musl targets.
 Two further hunks carried by the Node 20 patch set are no longer needed on
 Node 24 / V8 13:
  * condition-variable.cc was rewritten on top of Abseil, which selects the
    monotonic clock itself, so the pthread_condattr_setclock workaround is gone.
  * external-reference-table.cc now guards SYMBOLIZE_FUNCTION with
    V8_LIBC_GLIBC upstream.
--- a/deps/v8/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc
@@ -1261,7 +1261,7 @@
 #if V8_OS_DARWIN
     // Default on Mac OS X is 512kB -- bump up to 1MB
     stack_size = 1 * 1024 * 1024;
-#elif V8_OS_AIX
+#elif V8_OS_AIX || !defined(__GLIBC__)
     // Default on AIX is 96kB -- bump up to 2MB
     stack_size = 2 * 1024 * 1024;
 #endif
